# GitSync Rules

You are working on a compliant GitHub-to-LinkedIn visibility automation tool.

## Platform Policy

- Use official LinkedIn APIs only.
- Never scrape LinkedIn.
- Never automate LinkedIn website clicks.
- Never use unofficial Voyager endpoints.
- Never implement auto-like, auto-comment, auto-connect, auto-message, or engagement manipulation.
- LinkedIn profile Projects auto-editing is disabled unless explicit approved Profile Edit API access exists.

## GitHub Webhooks

- Always verify `X-Hub-Signature-256` with HMAC-SHA256.
- Store GitHub delivery IDs and make processing idempotent.
- Do webhook work asynchronously through queues.

## Content Generation

- Generate structured JSON before writing final post text.
- Every claim must map to GitHub evidence or explicit user input.
- Do not invent metrics, clients, users, revenue, production usage, or collaborators.
- Avoid generic AI phrases.

## Architecture

- Keep domain logic in `packages/domain`.
- Keep integrations in `packages/integrations`.
- Keep UI primitives in `packages/ui`.
- Keep API controllers thin.
- Keep worker processors idempotent.

## Security

- Encrypt tokens at rest.
- Never log OAuth tokens or webhook secrets.
- Minimize private repo content storage.
- Add audit logs to publishing and integration changes.

